<title>FRANCE: LVMH ready to study tax cost of drinks deal.</title>
<headline>LVMH ready to study tax cost of drinks deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton said on Friday it was willing to sit down with Guinness and Grand Metropolitan to study ways to minimise the tax costs of a demerger of the British groups' food and brewing units to create a three-way drinks merger.</p>
<p>The British companies said in a statement rejecting LVMH's proposal earlier on Friday that the plan would result in tax costs of 1.5 billion pounds.</p>
<p>&quot;LVMH is ready to study solutions with Guinness and Grand Metropolitan to minimise fiscal charges, with solutions of this sort having been found for past sales,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
</text>
